# Shamanic Journey (Theta Drum) — ~30 min — settle 8 Hz -> descend to 4.5 Hz drum -> journey hold -> callback 4.5->9 -> wake 10
# Goal: a shamanic "drum journey": a monotonous theta drum carries the listener down into a
#       lower/upper-world journey, then a faster "callback" rhythm brings them back. Scaffolding
#       for the practice, not a guarantee of any state.
# Basis: monotonous drumming at ~4-4.5 Hz (theta) is the classic driver of the "shamanic state of
#       consciousness". Melinda Maxfield found a steady ~4.5 Hz drum held for >=15 min reliably
#       shifts practitioners into theta trance (vivid imagery, time distortion); recent work links
#       theta neural tracking to drumming-induced altered states. Hence the ~4.5 Hz journey hold.
# Arc: settle ~8 Hz (warm) -> descend 8->4.5 Hz -> JOURNEY hold 4.5 Hz (14 min, steady sharp
#       isochronic drum) -> CALLBACK 4.5->9 Hz (the traditional faster recall that signals the
#       traveler to return) -> gentle wake to ~10 Hz + soft fade.
# Driver: ISOCHRONIC (the sharp, monotonous drum) via audio modulation = the pulse Hz; the pulse
#       slides by ramping mod directly (mod IS interpolatable, per guidelines 5a). Light flicker
#       runs 1:1 with the drum pulse.
# LED: dim warm amber square flicker tracking the drum 1:1 (all <=10 Hz, safe), gentle breathing
#       brightness LFO, four zones (mask 15).
# SAFETY: every rate <=10 Hz (below the 15-25 Hz photosensitive band); amber is NOT saturated red
#       (R/(R+G+B) = 220/340 = 0.65 < 0.8); no red<->blue; brightness capped <=30% with a floor;
#       light ramps in 20 s and fades out over the wake, never stopped abruptly. Eyes-closed,
#       lying down. Not a medical device; do not use if photosensitive/epileptic. Stop if unwell.
#
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (5a): the > prefix sits on the row where a segment BEGINS;
# its value is the start; the target is the next same-channel/field row's value, swept over the gap.

# --- Settle (00:00-03:00, drum 8 Hz): warm amber, vol + light fade in ---
0 8 50 >0 220 120 0 10           # LED 8 Hz square flicker, warm amber, brightness ramps 0->22% over 20 s
A 0 160 0 >0 8 1                 # ch1 isochronic drum: 160 Hz tone pulsed at 8 Hz; vol fades 0->50 over 45 s
S 5000 default 47 "Find a comfortable place to lie down. Let the drum find its rhythm around you."
20000 8 50 22 220 120 0 10       # brightness reaches 22% (ramp-in >=15 s satisfied)
45000 8 50 ~12:30:12000 220 120 0 10   # breathing LFO engages: brightness sine 12<->30% over 12 s
A 45000 160 0 50 8 1             # vol settled 50 (~45 s fade-in); drum steady 8 Hz

# --- Descent to the drumming theta (03:00-08:00, pulse 8->4.5 Hz, ~0.7 Hz/min) ---
A 180000 160 0 50 >8 1           # isochronic pulse ramp START 8 -> (target 4.5 at 08:00)
180000 >8 50 ~12:30:12000 220 120 0 10   # LED flicker tracks drum 8->4.5, breathing continues
S 180000 default 47 "Let the drum carry you downward, into the journey."

# --- Journey hold (08:00-22:00 = 14 min, pulse 4.5 Hz): the monotonous shamanic drum ---
A 480000 160 0 55 4.5 1          # steady 4.5 Hz isochronic drum (Maxfield's ~4.5 Hz theta trance); fuller vol
480000 4.5 50 ~12:30:12000 220 120 0 10   # warm amber, 4.5 Hz square flicker 1:1, gentle breathing LFO
S 480000 default 47 "You are in the between-place now. Let the steady drum hold you. Explore."
S 960000 default 47 "Wander freely. The drum is your thread home; it will not let you lose your way."

# --- Callback: the drummer's faster recall to return (22:00-26:00, pulse 4.5->9 Hz) ---
A 1320000 160 0 55 >4.5 1        # CALLBACK: isochronic pulse ramp START 4.5 -> (target 9 at 26:00), the recall
1320000 >4.5 50 22 220 120 0 10  # LED 4.5->9 lockstep; steady 22% for the alerting callback (LFO dropped)
S 1320000 default 47 "The drum is calling you back. Begin to return, following the quickening beat."

# --- Gentle wake (26:00-30:00, pulse 9->10 Hz) + soft fade ---
A 1560000 160 0 >55 >9 1         # pulse 9->10 (waking alpha); vol begins easing 55->0 over the wake
1560000 >9 50 >22 220 120 0 10   # LED 9->10; brightness gently fades 22->0
S 1560000 default 47 "Come fully back to the room. Feel the ground beneath you, and open your eyes when ready."
A 1800000 160 0 0 10 1           # end: volume 0, pulse settled at 10 Hz
1800000 10 50 0 220 120 0 10     # end: brightness 0
